Package: link
Title: Develop, Test and Communicate Intrinsic Habitat Models for Stream
    Networks
Version: 0.65.1
Date: 2026-10-15
Authors@R: c(
    person("Allan", "Irvine", , "al@newgraphenvironment.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-3495-2128")),
    person("Simon", "Norris", role = "ctb"),
    person("New Graph Environment Ltd.", role = c("cph", "fnd")))
Description: Tools for developing, testing and communicating intrinsic
    habitat models on stream networks: where each fish species could spawn
    and rear, and which of that habitat fish can reach. Current models
    rate habitat from stream gradient, channel width and discharge,
    resolve access past natural barriers, and record the road and rail
    crossings and dams below each reach. Every rule and threshold is a row
    in a config, so models can be changed, compared, checked against fish
    observations and traced to the rules that produced them. Runs on the
    British Columbia Freshwater Atlas through 'fresh'. Experimental: APIs
    and outputs change without notice.
